      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T21:35:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But if we are using the sensor in S0 and S3 (accelerometer for lid angle for instance), we will still see the error.",
      "revId": "1272715bb3d2ae520cef48209ad751ffe57bfff7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49814ccb_4f5d4151",
        "filename": "common/motion_sense.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 435,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T21:43:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We won\u0027t and don\u0027t see the error in S0 or true S3 because we have power to the sensors. The issue is that we\u0027re doing this:\n\nS0 -\u003e S3 (HOOK_CHIPSET_SUSPEND) -\u003e S5 (HOOK_CHIPSET_SHUTDOWN) \n\nThe hardware has already sequenced down. The EC\u0027s state machine is still reacting as we these indicator signals are asynchronous w.r.t. the EC.",
      "revId": "1272715bb3d2ae520cef48209ad751ffe57bfff7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57c0994a_c7a65fa6",
        "filename": "common/motion_sense.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 435,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T23:54:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To avoid any i2c errors when we entering S5, we should have set the sensor state to SENSOR_NOT_INITIALIZED while still in S0, otherwise motion_sense task would trigger some while reading the sensors just before HOOK_CHIPSET_SHUTDOWN hook is executed.\n\nShould have something like EC_CMD_HOST_SLEEP_EVENT when going to S5 where we can tell the EC ahead of time the power is going out? We could trigger HOOK_CHIPSET_SHUTDOWN on it.",
      "revId": "1272715bb3d2ae520cef48209ad751ffe57bfff7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c9f8cb8_f1eebe2f",
        "filename": "common/motion_sense.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 531,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T21:35:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the assumption is the sensor are still powered when we are executing HOOK_CHIPSET_SHUTDOWN hook.\nFrom include/hooks.h, the doc says:\n\nSystem is shutting down.  All suspend rails are still on.",
      "revId": "1272715bb3d2ae520cef48209ad751ffe57bfff7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad74cad9_c2c4304d",
        "filename": "common/motion_sense.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 531,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T21:43:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s not true, sadly. The comment is wrong and is largely dependent on the platform design. For x86 systems where we don\u0027t proxy S3_L or S5_L to the power control these states happen asynchronously. I actually don\u0027t know any system I\u0027ve worked on where the EC had control over those to make that comment valid.",
      "revId": "1272715bb3d2ae520cef48209ad751ffe57bfff7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
